                                                    PROJECT REPORT – 3
                                        Online E-Commerce Website Using Agile Methodology
1. Introduction

The Online E-Commerce Website is a web-based application that allows users to browse products, place orders, and manage purchases through an online platform. The system provides a convenient way for customers to shop anytime and helps businesses manage products and orders digitally.

This project is developed using the Agile Methodology, which supports flexible development, continuous improvement, and quick adaptation to changing business needs.

2. Problem Statement

Traditional shopping methods require physical presence and manual billing processes, which can be time-consuming and inefficient. Managing inventory and customer orders manually may lead to errors and poor customer experience. There is a need for an automated e-commerce system that enables secure, fast, and reliable online shopping.

3. Objectives of the Project

To provide an online shopping platform
To automate product and order management
To reduce manual billing and errors
To improve customer convenience
To maintain accurate sales records

4. Scope of the Project

The e-commerce website supports user registration, product browsing, cart management, order placement, and order history. Administrators can manage products, categories, orders, and users through an admin panel.

5. Agile Methodology

Agile methodology emphasizes iterative development, collaboration, and continuous feedback. The e-commerce system is developed in multiple sprints, with each sprint delivering a usable and tested feature.

Agile Practices Followed

Incremental development
Continuous integration and testing
Regular stakeholder feedback
Adaptive planning

6. Agile Development Process

Sprint 1
Requirement analysis
User registration and login

Sprint 2
Product listing and category management
Search functionality

Sprint 3
Shopping cart and order placement
Order history module

Sprint 4
Admin dashboard
System testing and deployment

